# rescue while already fighting. In the temple square (3005), Smokegod (60) sets Heroic's (51) skills to 100, and
# Locksmith (30) follows Heroic, in his group. Smokegod sets one cityguard (3060) on Heroic and another on Locksmith,
# and Heroic, fighting the first, rescues Locksmith from the second. Stock let him: set_fighting logged "Set_fighting:
# already fighting", Heroic went on fighting the first guard, and the second turned on him, fought by two and fighting
# one (#55). Now rescue refuses: "You're busy fighting!". Smokegod stats Heroic and both guards after, so their
# "Fighting:" lines show who fights whom. (Not @log: under --sanitize, the log also has UBSan's reports on stock's
# alloc_mem, whose blocks aren't aligned for pointers, #104.)
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect lock
Locksmith
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect hero
Heroic
psswrd
@return
@return
@as god
set skill heroic all 100
transfer heroic 3005
transfer locksmith 3005
goto 3005
@as lock
follow heroic
@as hero
group locksmith
@as god
@mob 3060 3005
@mob 3060 3005
force 1.cityguard kill heroic
force 2.cityguard kill locksmith
@as hero
rescue locksmith
@as god
stat heroic
stat 1.cityguard
stat 2.cityguard
